  "findings": [
    "The Tiny Tapeout 2025.10.29_01.10 and ChipFoundry 2026.03.30_01.00 native decks both return zero markers on counter, UART and APB with FEOL, BEOL and off-grid enabled.",
    "These decks share upstream provenance. Output-label changes from the older 2022 deck include renames and are not counted as new physical coverage.",
    "The Tiny Tapeout version reports zero contact-coverage markers for an uncovered mcon inside areaid:core (81:2); ChipFoundry and the existing Studio ct.4 predicate each report one.",
    "Outside core, both decks detect the uncovered contact; covered contact controls pass the coverage predicate with and without core.",
    "The new Studio regression covers absent, enclosing and crossing core markers, a one-nm uncovered strip, and fill that must not substitute for a drawn conductor.",
    "The first trial used the wrong marker (81:10); its assertion failed. Corrected v2 uses 81:2. Failed outputs are retained and excluded from accepted controls.",
    "The copied decks retain explicit GPLv3 file headers and the full license. No Apache root license is substituted, and no later-version grant is inferred."
  ],
